# VGA Animation Top-Level

## Overview
This project provides the top-level VGA structure for an animation-based graphics design on FPGA.

The module connects the FPGA board to a VGA monitor through the `vga_adapter` module. It configures a 160x120 VGA display and prepares the required signals for drawing animated pixels or shapes on the screen.

## Functionality
- Connects the 50 MHz board clock to the VGA controller
- Uses KEY[0] as the reset input
- Instantiates the VGA adapter module
- Configures the VGA resolution to 160x120
- Defines the main drawing signals: x, y, color, and writeEn
- Provides the structure needed for implementing animation logic

## Important Note
This file is mainly a top-level template.  
The actual animation logic must generate the x-coordinate, y-coordinate, color, and write enable signals.
